Force-inline encoder helpers to reduce stack use per nesting level

In optimized builds, marking encode_field(), encode_scalar() and
encode_array() as UPB_FORCEINLINE makes encoding a nested message use one
stack frame (encode_message) per nesting level instead of two, cutting encoder
stack use per level by ~25-28% (e.g. 192 -> 144 bytes on arm64 at -O3 for
chains like "a + b + ..."). Inlining only encode_scalar() makes things worse
(encode_field() then gets outlined), so all three are needed.

This is only done when optimizing (__OPTIMIZE__): in unoptimized builds the
inlined functions' locals don't share stack slots, which increases stack use
per level instead (e.g. 1885 -> 3464 bytes at -O0). No effect on MSVC, where
UPB_FORCEINLINE is plain "static" and __OPTIMIZE__ isn't defined.

--- a/upb.c
+++ b/upb.c
@@ -9854,7 +9854,17 @@
